3. ASSUMPTIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The following assumptions were applied during data preparation and
KPI definition. They are documented assumptions, not facts about
the original data source.

A1  SLA target days by severity (ITIL-style assumed tiers):
      Critical = 2 days
      High     = 5 days
      Medium   = 10 days
      Low      = 20 days

A2  Severity mapping (source → cleaned):
      "Severity 1" → Critical
      "Severity 2" → High
      "Severity 3" → Medium
      "Severity 4" → Low

A3  Null Status values (104 rows) inferred from the Is_Closed flag:
      Is_Closed=1 → Status = "Closed"
      Is_Closed=0 → Status = "Open"

A4  "Re-open" standardised to "Re-Opened"; treated as Open for
    KPI counting purposes.

A5  "Deferred" defects are tracked in a separate KPI
    ([Deferred Defects]) and excluded from both Open and Closed counts.

A6  High Risk defined as Risk_Score ≥ 15
    (standard red-zone on a 5×5 probability × impact matrix).

A7  Dim_Date calendar spans 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31 to cover
    all data with a one-year future buffer.
